## Installation
[% if project_type == 'home-assistant' %]
[![Open the repository in HACS](https://my.home-assistant.io/badges/hacs_repository.svg)](https://my.home-assistant.io/redirect/hacs_repository/?owner={= owner =}&repository={= project_slug =}&category=integration)

1. In HACS, add `https://github.com/{= repo =}` as a custom repository of the type *Integration*, or use the button above.
2. Download **{= project_name =}** and restart Home Assistant.
3. Add the integration under *Settings → Devices & services → Add integration*.
[% elif project_type == 'nextcloud-app' %]
Install **{= project_name =}** from the [Nextcloud App Store](https://apps.nextcloud.com/apps/{= nextcloud_app_id =}): as an administrator, under *Apps*, or with

```sh
php occ app:install {= nextcloud_app_id =}
```
[% elif project_type == 'github-action' %]
```yaml
- uses: {= repo =}@<commit-hash> # vX.Y.Z
  with:
    name: World
```

Pin the action to the commit hash of a [release](https://github.com/{= repo =}/releases); Dependabot or Renovate then keeps it current.
[% elif project_type == 'python-package' %]
```sh
pip install {= project_slug =}
```
[% elif project_type == 'node-package' %]
```sh
npm install {= project_slug =}
```
[% elif project_type == 'container' %]
```sh
docker run --rm ghcr.io/{= repo | lower =}:latest
```

Every image carries its SBOM and a signed provenance attestation:

```sh
gh attestation verify oci://ghcr.io/{= repo | lower =}:latest --owner {= owner =}
```
